1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,542
Chapter fourteen — make it yours.

2
00:00:03,602 --> 00:00:16,101
Everything the workbench knows
is a registry you can edit.

3
00:00:16,161 --> 00:00:28,106
Plugins is the whole catalog: node types, expert personas,
chassis, protocols, deploy targets, SKUs, skills.

4
00:00:28,166 --> 00:00:49,722
Nearly three hundred entries across eight
registries — and you can add your own.

5
00:00:49,782 --> 00:00:55,326
Skill cards are what the AI
reads about each component.

6
00:00:55,386 --> 00:01:14,090
Dials, defaults, failure modes and sizing
rules — the same card an expert is handed.

7
00:01:14,150 --> 00:01:30,797
The service catalog rolls a design up into
business services — process, people and software.

8
00:01:30,857 --> 00:01:44,950
And the Field Manual is the guided
walkthrough of the whole workbench.

9
00:01:45,010 --> 00:01:54,255
Settings is provider, model, reasoning
effort and your default cloud.

10
00:01:54,315 --> 00:02:11,063
Anthropic in the cloud, or anything OpenAI-compatible
— including a model on your own machine.

11
00:02:11,123 --> 00:02:20,569
Local AI checks your hardware and
picks a model that actually fits in it.

12
00:02:20,629 --> 00:02:31,074
It reads the GPU, the unified memory and the
cores, then recommends and configures the runtime.

13
00:02:31,134 --> 00:02:42,470
Ollama or LM Studio, entirely on your
machine — nothing leaves the building.

14
00:02:42,530 --> 00:02:50,258
One more thing.

15
00:02:50,318 --> 00:03:00,265
Zen Mode — the temple, the
laws of scale, and a yeti.

16
00:03:00,325 --> 00:03:11,178
Because a tool you enjoy opening
is a tool you keep using.

17
00:03:11,238 --> 00:03:15,181
That is the workbench, end to end.

18
00:03:15,241 --> 00:03:19,843
Vibecode with the whole system in view.
